\"b\", \"3\", \"b\", \"0\", \"2\", \"7\", \"e\", \"f\", \"0\", \"c\", \"d\", \"3\", \"2\", \"2\", \"b\", \"f\", \"a\", \"8\", \"3\", \"9\", \"b\", \"9\", \"a\", \"a\", \"f\", \"5\", \"b\", \"2\", \"7\", \"5\", \"5\", \"1\", \"e\", \"e\", \"a\", \"5\", \"4\", \"c\", \"f\", \"6\", \"h\", \"t\", \"t\", \"p\", \"s\", \":\", \"/\", \"/\", \"g\", \"i\", \"t\", \".\", \"k\", \"e\", \"r\", \"n\", \"e\", \"l\", \".\", \"o\", \"r\", \"g\", \"/\", \"s\", \"t\", \"a\", \"b\", \"l\", \"e\", \"/\", \"c\", \"/\", \"e\", \"3\", \"f\", \"3\", \"3\", \"b\", \"0\", \"a\", \"1\", \"d\", \"8\", \"9\", \"d\", \"7\", \"3\", \"8\", \"e\", \"2\", \"b\", \"9\", \"1\", \"3\", \"d\", \"a\", \"b\", \"5\", \"1\", \"9\", \"2\", \"2\", \"6\", \"e\", \"a\", \"f\", \"7\", \"6\", \"e\", \"1\", \"5\", \"b\", \"h\", \"t\", \"t\", \"p\", \":\", \"/\", \"/\", \"w\", \"w\", \"w\", \".\", \"o\", \"p\", \"e\", \"n\", \"w\", \"a\", \"l\", \"l\", \".\", \"c\", \"o\", \"m\", \"/\", \"l\", \"i\", \"s\", \"t\", \"s\", \"/\", \"o\", \"s\", \"s\", \"-\", \"s\", \"e\", \"c\", \"u\", \"r\", \"i\", \"t\", \"y\", \"/\", \"2\", \"0\", \"2\", \"6\", \"/\", \"1\", \"0\", \"/\", \"3\", \"0\", \"/\", \"1\", \"h\", \"t\", \"t\", \"p\", \":\", \"/\", \"/\", \"w\", \"w\", \"w\", \".\", \"o\", \"p\", \"e\", \"n\", \"w\", \"a\", \"l\", \"l\", \".\", \"c\", \"o\", \"m\", \"/\", \"l\", \"i\", \"s\", \"t\", \"s\", \"/\", \"o\", \"s\", \"s\", \"-\", \"s\", \"e\", \"c\", \"u\", \"r\", \"i\", \"t\", \"y\", \"/\", \"2\", \"0\", \"2\", \"6\", \"/\", \"1\", \"0\", \"/\", \"3\", \"0\", \"/\", \"6\"]}\n        ```\n    *   **搜索引擎结果：**\n        ```\n        \n        ```\n    *   **漏洞利用代码：**\n        ```\n        /tmp/c008dfc8931cd1aead48fe186bcec072/LICENSE\n---\nMIT License\n\nCopyright (c) 2026 Alucard0x1\n\nPermission is hereby granted, free of charge, to any person obtaining a copy\nof this software and associated documentation files (the \"Software\"), to deal\nin the Software without restriction, including without limitation the rights\nto use, copy, modify, merge, publish, distribute, sublicense, and/or sell\ncopies of the Software, and to permit persons to whom the Software is\nfurnished to do so, subject to the following conditions:\n\nThe above copyright notice and this permission notice shall be included in all\ncopies or substantial portions of the Software.\n\nTHE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED \"AS IS\", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR\nIMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY,\nFITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE AND NONINFRINGEMENT. IN NO EVENT SHALL THE\nAUTHORS OR COPYRIGHT HOLDERS BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES OR OTHER\nLIABILITY, WHETHER IN AN ACTION OF CONTRACT, TORT OR OTHERWISE, ARISING FROM,\nOUT OF OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE SOFTWARE OR THE USE OR OTHER DEALINGS IN THE\nSOFTWARE.\n\n\n---\n/tmp/c008dfc8931cd1aead48fe186bcec072/README.md\n---\n# CVE-2026-98432 — Linux IPv4/TCP `ireq_opt` use-after-free PoC\n\nProof-only proof of concept for CVE-2026-98432 (CVSS 9.8): a remotely\ntriggerable use-after-free in the Linux IPv4/TCP stack.\n\n**For authorized security testing only.** Run it against systems you own or\nhave explicit permission to test.\n\n---\n\n## What it proves\n\nThe PoC triggers the race and detects when the kernel copies bytes out of a\nfreed `ip_options_rcu` object into a SYN-ACK. It **does not** create users or\nfiles, and it does **not** implement a code-execution chain.\n\nA hit means the server returned another allocation's marker inside its\nSYN-ACK — a correct kernel cannot do that. In a controlled test on Ubuntu\n24.04.5 with kernel `6.8.0-147-generic` (listed vulnerable by Ubuntu; fix\nqueued in `6.8.0-149`), a 180-second loopback run produced **21 hits in\n320,829 attempts**, and a 300-second run produced **22 hits in 616,911\nattempts**. The kernel stayed clean (`tainted=0`, no oops).\n\nNo packet captures or logs from that host are included here; the PoC's own\noutput is the evidence.\n\n---\n\n## 1. The bug\n\nA SYN carrying IPv4 options makes the kernel build an `ip_options_rcu`\n(72 bytes, `kmalloc-96`) for the request socket. When the handshake completes,\n`tcp_v4_syn_recv_sock()` hands that object to the child socket **without\ncopying it**, then clears the pointer in the request socket. A second CPU that\nalready looked the request socket up can still be inside\n`tcp_check_req()` → `tcp_v4_send_synack()` → `ip_build_and_send_pkt()` →\n`ip_options_build()`, reading the same object. Child sockets are not\n`SOCK_RCU_FREE`, and `inet_sock_destruct()` frees `inet_opt` with a plain\n`kfree()`, so if the child is torn down in that window the reader dereferences\nfreed memory.\n\nA second variant exists with request-socket migration\n(`net.ipv4.tcp_migrate_req=1` or a BPF reuseport program); the fix uses\n`kfree_rcu()` in both `inet_sock_destruct()` and `tcp_v4_reqsk_destructor()`.\n\nIntroduced in Linux 4.4 (`079096f103fa`); fixed in mainline 7.3 and\nbackported to 5.10.272, 5.15.223, 6.1.190, 6.6.159, 6.12.113, 6.18.56 and\n7.2.10. Affected: Linux 4.4 and later, unpatched.\n\nImpact ranges from a remote crash (DoS) to kernel memory disclosure and, with\na full exploit chain, code execution. This repository stops at proving the\nuse-after-free.\n\n---\n\n## 2. How the PoC works\n\nPer attempt:\n\n1. **SYN** with a 40-byte IPv4 Timestamp option (or Record Route) → request\n   socket with `ireq_opt`; the target echoes the option in its SYN-ACK.\n2. **Duplicate pure SYN** sent just before the handshake ACK, so a second CPU\n   runs the SYN-ACK path against the request socket.\n3. **ACK** completes the handshake; the child inherits `inet_opt`, the request\n   socket drops its pointer.\n4. **RST** (with ACK, so it survives the local RST filter) tears the child\n   down, freeing the object while the duplicate-SYN reader may still be using\n   it.\n\n**Oracle.** Every attempt embeds a unique 32-bit magic plus a check tag at\noption offsets 16..23. Three rewrites happen before a user-space reader sees\nthe option:\n\n| stage | slot |\n|---|---|\n| server `ip_options_compile()` on the SYN | 4..7 (TS) / 3..6 (RR) |\n| server `ip_options_build()` for the SYN-ACK | 8..11 (TS) / 7..10 (RR) |\n| receiving host `ip_options_compile()` on the SYN-ACK | 12..15 (TS) / 11..14 (RR) |\n\nThe marker lives past all three. A SYN-ACK that echoes a *different*\nallocation's magic (with `tag == magic ^ 0x5a5a5a5a`) proves the reader copied\nfrom a freed-and-reused object.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Requirements\n\n- Linux, root or `CAP_NET_RAW`; the automatic RST filter needs\n  `CAP_NET_ADMIN` (root).\n- Target: unpatched Linux with an IPv4 TCP listener that `accept()`s.\n- Python 3.8+ (tested on 3.12), standard library only.\n- `iptables`/nftables for the bare-RST filter.\n\n`--proof` is self-con\n        ```\n\n    **你的角色：** 你是一名专业的网络安全分析师，擅长分析CVE漏洞信息。\n\n    **任务：**\n\n    1.  **CVE有效性：** 分析此CVE是否为真实存在的有效漏洞。请综合考虑CVE编号格式、漏洞描述的完整性、参考链接的存在、漏洞的技术细节等因素。\n    2.  **POC有效性：** 判断提供的POC代码是否有效，是否能实际利用此漏洞，并分析其有效性。\n    3.  **投毒风险：** 分析POC代码内容,判断此仓库中是否存在作者隐藏的投毒代码,分析结果使用百分比。务必不要把POC验证的后门代码判定为投毒代码。\n    4.  **利用方式：** 详细分析并总结漏洞的利用方式，包括攻击步骤、所需条件等。\n    5.  **代码分析：** 详细分析POC代码的工作原理、关键组件和执行流程。\n    6.  **排序优先级:** 搜索引擎结果 >  漏洞利用代码 > 漏洞库信息\n    7.  **输出内容:** 务必使用中文\n    8.  **markdown内容:** 务必使用markdown格式，包含以下部分：\n        - 漏洞概述\n        - 有效性分析\n        - 投毒风险分析\n        - 利用方式\n        - 代码分析\n    **输出格式：**  你**必须**严格按照以下 **JSON** 格式输出，**不要包含任何额外的文字、说明或前缀/后缀**。JSON中的**所有键和字符串类型的值必须使用双引号**。请务必对特殊字符进行转义。\n\n    **示例JSON:**```json\n    {\n        \"name\": \"CVE-2023-12345-ExampleApp-SQL注入\",\n        \"type\": \"SQL注入\",\n        \"app\": \"ExampleApp\", \n        \"risk\": \"高危，可能导致数据泄露和远程代码执行\",\n        \"version\": \"<= 1.0\",\n        \"condition\": \"需要网络访问和数据库端口开放\",\n        \"poc_available\": \"是\",\n        \"poison\": \"90%\",\n        \"cve_valid\": \"是\",\n        \"markdown\": \"# 漏洞概述\n\n该漏洞存在于ExampleApp的登录模块,攻击者可以通过构造恶意的SQL语句绕过身份验证...\n\n## 有效性分析\n\n根据CVE编号格式、漏洞描述的完整性、参考链接的存在等因素，该CVE是真实有效的...\n\n## 投毒风险分析\n\n该仓库存在较高的投毒风险，主要原因是...\n\n## 利用方式\n\n1.  攻击者需要网络访问权限\n2.  构造恶意的SQL语句\n3.  发送到目标系统\n4.  绕过身份验证，获取系统访问权限\n\n## 代码分析\n\n主要代码组件包括：\n- `exploit.py`: 主漏洞利用脚本\n- `payloads.py`: 包含各种SQL注入payload\n- `utils.py`: 辅助工具函数\n\n代码执行流程：\n1.  连接到目标数据库\n2.  构造恶意SQL语句\n3.  发送到目标系统\n4.  解析响应，获取敏感信息\n\",\n        \"repo_name\": \"example/repo\",\n        \"repo_url\": \"https://github.com/example/repo\",\n        \"cve_url\": \"https://cve.mitre.org/cgi-bin/cvename.cgi?name=CVE-2023-12345\"\n    }\n        ",
