    "prompt": "\n      请根据以下漏洞信息、搜索结果和漏洞利用代码，生成一份详细的漏洞分析报告，包含有效性分析、投毒风险分析、利用方式、代码分析等内容。请注意以下几点：\n\n    **信息来源：**\n\n    *   **漏洞库信息：**\n        ```\n        {\"cve_id\": \"CVE-2026-116244\", \"sources\": [\"NVD\", \"OSCS\"], \"descriptions\": [\"When a pgAdmin 4 connection was not meant to use a Kerberos user's delegated credentials, pgAdmin removed KRB5CCNAME from its environment, so the Kerberos library fell back to the default credential cache, or a client keytab, of the operating-system account running pgAdmin. libpq then answered any server that asked for GSSAPI authentication with that account's ticket, whatever user name the pgAdmin user gave, so in server mode any user could connect as the service account's Kerberos principal; gssencmode=disable did not prevent it. On Windows, SSPI used the service account's logon in the same way. psql was also started with pgAdmin's environment, which could hold another user's credential cache while that user was connecting.\\n\\nThe fix points KRB5CCNAME and KRB5_CLIENT_KTNAME at a file that cannot exist except while a Kerberos-authenticated user connects with Kerberos, and gives every other connection, psql and the utilities require_auth=!gss,!sspi and gssencmode=disable, checked on the final connection string. require_auth needs libpq 16 or later.\\n\\nThis issue affects pgAdmin 4: before 9.19.\", \"\\u6807\\u9898: pgAdmin 4 Kerberos\\u51ed\\u636e\\u6cc4\\u9732\\u6f0f\\u6d1e\"], \"published_date\": \"2026-10-30T20:17:04.327\", \"last_modified_date\": \"2026-10-30T20:17:04.327\", \"cvss_score\": 8.2, \"severity\": \"HIGH\", \"references\": [\"h\", \"t\", \"t\", \"p\", \"s\", \":\", \"/\", \"/\", \"g\", \"i\", \"t\", \"h\", \"u\", \"b\", \".\", \"c\", \"o\", \"m\", \"/\", \"p\", \"g\", \"a\", \"d\", \"m\", \"i\", \"n\", \"-\", \"o\", \"r\", \"g\", \"/\", \"p\", \"g\", \"a\", \"d\", \"m\", \"i\", \"n\", \"4\", \"/\", \"c\", \"o\", \"m\", \"m\", \"i\", \"t\", \"/\", \"1\", \"4\", \"5\", \"e\", \"5\", \"1\", \"1\", \"f\", \"0\", \"5\", \"e\", \"e\", \"d\", \"6\", \"9\", \"e\", \"b\", \"c\", \"a\", \"d\", \"d\", \"3\", \"c\", \"d\", \"6\", \"1\", \"f\", \"f\", \"e\", \"a\", \"0\", \"a\", \"5\", \"b\", \"4\", \"c\", \"6\", \"9\", \"a\", \"4\", \"h\", \"t\", \"t\", \"p\", \"s\", \":\", \"/\", \"/\", \"g\", \"i\", \"t\", \"h\", \"u\", \"b\", \".\", \"c\", \"o\", \"m\", \"/\", \"p\", \"g\", \"a\", \"d\", \"m\", \"i\", \"n\", \"-\", \"o\", \"r\", \"g\", \"/\", \"p\", \"g\", \"a\", \"d\", \"m\", \"i\", \"n\", \"4\", \"/\", \"i\", \"s\", \"s\", \"u\", \"e\", \"s\", \"/\", \"1\", \"0\", \"6\", \"5\", \"5\"]}\n        ```\n    *   **搜索引擎结果：**\n        ```\n        \n            ## 以下内容是基于此漏洞的搜索结果:\n                [webpage 0 begin] [title] CVE-2026-116244 - Exploits & Severity - Feedly\n [description] This CVE ID has been reserved by a CNA but the vulnerability details have not yet been published. Feedly AI found some discussions about it.\n [link] https://feedly.com/cve/CVE-2026-116244\n [webpage 0 end]\n[webpage 1 begin] [title] GitHub - 0xMarcio/pocindex: Search public CVE proof-of-concept exploits ...\n [description] PoC Index: Search public CVE proof-of-concept exploits from GitHub, Nuclei, ExploitDB, Metasploit and Vulhub, with CVSS, EPSS and CISA KEV context. Find exploits by CVE, vendor, product or keyword.\n [link] https://github.com/0xMarcio/pocindex\n [webpage 1 end]\n[webpage 2 begin] [title] CVE-2026-116244: pgAdmin 4 Vulnerability (CVSS 8.2) | CVETodo\n [description] CVE-2026-116244 is a CVSS 8.2 high-severity vulnerability in pgAdmin 4. Includes technical details, affected versions, and mitigation steps.\n [link] https://cvetodo.com/cve/CVE-2026-116244\n [webpage 2 end]\n[webpage 3 begin] [title] CVE-2026-106244: Google Chrome Auth Bypass Vulnerability\n [description] CVE-2026-106244 is an authorization bypass vulnerability in Google Chrome. Learn about its impact, affected versions, and mitigation methods.\n [link] https://www.sentinelone.com/vulnerability-database/cve-2026-106244/\n [webpage 3 end]\n[webpage 4 begin] [title] GitHub - Mr-xn/Penetration_Testing_POC: 渗透测试有关的POC、EXP、脚本、提权、小工具等 ...\n [description] 渗透测试有关的POC、EXP、脚本、提权、小工具等---About penetration-testing python-script poc getshell csrf xss cms php-getshell domainmod-xss csrf-webshell cobub-razor cve rce sql sql-poc poc-exp bypass oa-getshell cve...\n [link] https://github.com/Mr-xn/Penetration_Testing_POC\n [webpage 4 end]\n[webpage 5 begin] [title] Common Vulnerabilities and Exposures - Wikipedia\n [description] MITRE Corporation's documentation defines CVE Identifiers (also called \"CVE names\", \"CVE numbers\", \"CVE-IDs\", and \"CVEs\") as unique, common identifiers for publicly known information-security vulnerabilities in publicly released software packages.\n [link] https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Common_Vulnerabilities_and_Exposures\n [webpage 5 end]\n[webpage 6 begin] [title] CVE: Common Vulnerabilities and Exposures\n [description] Identify, define, and catalog publicly disclosed cybersecurity vulnerabilities. There are currently over 398,000 CVE Records accessible via Download or Keyword Search above. The CVE Program partners with community members worldwide to grow CVE content and expand its usage.\n [link] https://www.cve.org/\n [webpage 6 end]\n[webpage 7 begin] [title] CVE: Common Vulnerabilities and Exposures\n [description] There is one CVE Record for each vulnerability on the CVE List. Vulnerabilities are first discovered, then reported to the CVE Program. The reporter requests a CVE ID, which is then reserved for the reported vulnerability.\n [link] https://www.cve.org/About/Process\n [webpage 7 end]\n[webpage 8 begin] [title] CVEs and Security Vulnerabilities - OpenCVE\n [description] 7 hours ago · Difficult to exploit vulnerability allows unauthenticated attacker with network access via HTTP to compromise Oracle HTTP Server. While the vulnerability is in Oracle HTTP Server, attacks may significantly impact additional products (scope change).\n [link] https://app.opencve.io/\n [webpage 8 end]\n[webpage 9 begin] [title] Known Exploited Vulnerabilities Catalog - CISA\n [description] For the benefit of the cybersecurity community and network defenders—and to help every organization better manage vulnerabilities and keep pace with threat activity—CISA maintains the authoritative source of vulnerabilities that have been exploited in the wild.\n [link] https://www.cisa.gov/known-exploited-vulnerabilities-catalog\n [webpage 9 end]\n\n            \n        ```\n    *   **漏洞利用代码：**\n        ```\n        /tmp/6c02c2d0f9c00855ff9111340bc29a8f/CITATION.cff\n---\ncff-version: 1.2.0\nmessage: \"If this PoC helped you, cite it as below.\"\ntitle: \"CVE-2026-116244: pgAdmin 4 service-account Kerberos credential leak — PoC\"\nauthors:\n  - alias: googlesky\ntype: software\nkeywords:\n  - CVE-2026-116244\n  - pgAdmin\n  - kerberos\n  - gssapi\n  - security\n  - proof-of-concept\nlicense: MIT\n\n\n---\n/tmp/6c02c2d0f9c00855ff9111340bc29a8f/LICENSE\n---\nMIT License\n\nCopyright (c) 2026 googlesky\n\nPermission is hereby granted, free of charge, to any person obtaining a copy\nof this software and associated documentation files (the \"Software\"), to deal\nin the Software without restriction, including without limitation the rights\nto use, copy, modify, merge, publish, distribute, sublicense, and/or sell\ncopies of the Software, and to permit persons to whom the Software is\nfurnished to do so, subject to the following conditions:\n\nThe above copyright notice and this permission notice shall be included in all\ncopies or substantial portions of the Software.\n\nTHE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED \"AS IS\", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR\nIMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY,\nFITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE AND NONINFRINGEMENT. IN NO EVENT SHALL THE\nAUTHORS OR COPYRIGHT HOLDERS BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES OR OTHER\nLIABILITY, WHETHER IN AN ACTION OF CONTRACT, TORT OR OTHERWISE, ARISING FROM,\nOUT OF OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE SOFTWARE OR THE USE OR OTHER DEALINGS IN THE\nSOFTWARE.\n\n\n---\n/tmp/6c02c2d0f9c00855ff9111340bc29a8f/README.md\n---\n# CVE-2026-116244 — pgAdmin 4 service-account Kerberos credential leak\n\n| | |\n|---|---|\n| **CVE** | CVE-2026-116244 |\n| **Product** | pgAdmin 4 (server mode) |\n| **Affected** | ≤ v9.18 |\n| **Fixed** | v9.19 (2026-10-29), [issue #10655](https://github.com/pgadmin-org/pgadmin4/issues/10655) |\n| **Class** | Ambient credential confusion / authentication bypass (CWE-668-ish) |\n| **Preconditions** | pgAdmin runs in **server mode**; the OS account running pgAdmin has Kerberos credentials reachable through the **default** credential cache (`/tmp/krb5cc_<uid>`) or the default/client keytab — exactly what happens when pgAdmin's host has been `kinit`-ed for the service account or uses a client keytab; attacker needs **any** pgAdmin web account (internal auth, no Kerberos); a PostgreSQL server reachable from the pgAdmin host that authenticates with **GSSAPI** (and maps the service principal to a privileged role — e.g. the pgAdmin service principal is also a DB superuser/owner). |\n| **Impact** | A low-privilege web user makes pgAdmin's libpq answer the database's GSSAPI challenge **as the pgAdmin service account's principal**, inheriting every privilege that principal has on that server. No password, no Kerberos login, one unauthenticated-to-DB click path. |\n\n## Root cause\n\nFor every server connection made on behalf of a web user, pgAdmin (≤ 9.18)\ntemporarily \"isolates\" Kerberos state in\n[`web/pgadmin/utils/locker.py`](web/pgadmin/utils/locker.py):\n\n```python\nif source == KERBEROS and 'KRB5CCNAME' in session and self.is_kerberos_conn:\n    environ['KRB5CCNAME'] = session['KRB5CCNAME']   # user's delegated ticket\nelse:\n    environ.pop('KRB5CCNAME', None)                 # <-- the bug\n```\n\nRemoving `KRB5CCNAME` does **not** remove Kerberos: libpq still answers a\nserver's `AuthenticationGSS` request, and the Kerberos library then falls back\nto the **default credential cache of the OS account running pgAdmin**\n(`/tmp/krb5cc_<uid>`) — or acquires one from the account's default client\nkeytab (`~/client.keytab`, `KRB5_CLIENT_KTNAME`). Whatever TGT the *service\naccount* holds is used for the GSS exchange, so the web user authenticates as\nthe *service principal* (e.g. `pgadminsvc@REALM`), and PostgreSQL's `pg_ident`\nmapping then logs them into the privileged role that principal maps to.\n\nThe connect itself is `psycopg.Connection.connect(...)` inside the locker\n(`web/pgadmin/utils/driver/psycopg3/connection.py`), so the credentials leak\nthrough pgAdmin's own driver path — and equally through psql/pg_dump, which\ninherit the same environment.\n\n## Fix (v9.19)\n\n`locker.py` now points the environment at a cache/keytab that can never exist\nand additionally hard-stops the GSS negotiation at the libpq level:\n\n```python\nNO_KERBEROS_CREDENTIALS = {\n    'KRB5CCNAME': 'FILE:' + NO_CLIENT_FILE,        # inside the app dir, never creatable\n    'KRB5_CLIENT_KTNAME': 'FILE:' + NO_CLIENT_FILE,\n}\n# plus, for every connection that may not use Kerberos:\n#   gssencmode=disable\n#   require_auth=!gss,!sspi     (libpq >= 16; blocks SSPI on Windows and gssproxy)\n# a server whose require_auth allows only gss/sspi is refused outright.\n```\n\nA user who actually logged in to pgAdmin **with** Kerberos still gets their own\ndelegated `KRB5CCNAME`, but only for servers with Kerberos authentication\nenabled.\n\n## The lab (fully containerized)\n\n```\n┌────────────┐   UDP/TCP 88    ┌───────────────────┐\n│    kdc     │◄───────────────►│  db (postgres:17)\n        ```\n\n    **你的角色：** 你是一名专业的网络安全分析师，擅长分析CVE漏洞信息。\n\n    **任务：**\n\n    1.  **CVE有效性：** 分析此CVE是否为真实存在的有效漏洞。请综合考虑CVE编号格式、漏洞描述的完整性、参考链接的存在、漏洞的技术细节等因素。\n    2.  **POC有效性：** 判断提供的POC代码是否有效，是否能实际利用此漏洞，并分析其有效性。\n    3.  **投毒风险：** 分析POC代码内容,判断此仓库中是否存在作者隐藏的投毒代码,分析结果使用百分比。务必不要把POC验证的后门代码判定为投毒代码。\n    4.  **利用方式：** 详细分析并总结漏洞的利用方式，包括攻击步骤、所需条件等。\n    5.  **代码分析：** 详细分析POC代码的工作原理、关键组件和执行流程。\n    6.  **排序优先级:** 搜索引擎结果 >  漏洞利用代码 > 漏洞库信息\n    7.  **输出内容:** 务必使用中文\n    8.  **markdown内容:** 务必使用markdown格式，包含以下部分：\n        - 漏洞概述\n        - 有效性分析\n        - 投毒风险分析\n        - 利用方式\n        - 代码分析\n    **输出格式：**  你**必须**严格按照以下 **JSON** 格式输出，**不要包含任何额外的文字、说明或前缀/后缀**。JSON中的**所有键和字符串类型的值必须使用双引号**。请务必对特殊字符进行转义。\n\n    **示例JSON:**```json\n    {\n        \"name\": \"CVE-2023-12345-ExampleApp-SQL注入\",\n        \"type\": \"SQL注入\",\n        \"app\": \"ExampleApp\", \n        \"risk\": \"高危，可能导致数据泄露和远程代码执行\",\n        \"version\": \"<= 1.0\",\n        \"condition\": \"需要网络访问和数据库端口开放\",\n        \"poc_available\": \"是\",\n        \"poison\": \"90%\",\n        \"cve_valid\": \"是\",\n        \"markdown\": \"# 漏洞概述\n\n该漏洞存在于ExampleApp的登录模块,攻击者可以通过构造恶意的SQL语句绕过身份验证...\n\n## 有效性分析\n\n根据CVE编号格式、漏洞描述的完整性、参考链接的存在等因素，该CVE是真实有效的...\n\n## 投毒风险分析\n\n该仓库存在较高的投毒风险，主要原因是...\n\n## 利用方式\n\n1.  攻击者需要网络访问权限\n2.  构造恶意的SQL语句\n3.  发送到目标系统\n4.  绕过身份验证，获取系统访问权限\n\n## 代码分析\n\n主要代码组件包括：\n- `exploit.py`: 主漏洞利用脚本\n- `payloads.py`: 包含各种SQL注入payload\n- `utils.py`: 辅助工具函数\n\n代码执行流程：\n1.  连接到目标数据库\n2.  构造恶意SQL语句\n3.  发送到目标系统\n4.  解析响应，获取敏感信息\n\",\n        \"repo_name\": \"example/repo\",\n        \"repo_url\": \"https://github.com/example/repo\",\n        \"cve_url\": \"https://cve.mitre.org/cgi-bin/cvename.cgi?name=CVE-2023-12345\"\n    }\n        ",
