    "prompt": "\n      请根据以下漏洞信息、搜索结果和漏洞利用代码，生成一份详细的漏洞分析报告，包含有效性分析、投毒风险分析、利用方式、代码分析等内容。请注意以下几点：\n\n    **信息来源：**\n\n    *   **漏洞库信息：**\n        ```\n        {\"cve_id\": \"CVE-2026-98260\", \"sources\": [\"NVD\", \"OSCS\"], \"descriptions\": [\"In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\\n\\nexec: Cleanup POSIX timers right after de_thread()\\n\\nA per-thread CPU timer holds a reference to the PID of the thread it is\\nattached to and, while it is armed, its node is queued in that thread's\\nposix_cputimers. The task is looked up by that PID.\\n\\nWhen a non-leader thread exec()s, de_thread() changes which task owns\\nthat PID. pid_task(timer->it.cpu.pid, PIDTYPE_PID) then returns NULL,\\nbut the node is still queued on tsk, which is alive. timer_lock_sighand()\\ntakes a failed lookup to mean that the node is already dequeued, so it\\nhas nothing to undo.\\n\\nbegin_new_exec() calls posix_cpu_timers_exit(me) right after\\nexec_task_namespaces() and that removes the leftover node, so the state\\nnormally stays invisible. But bprm->point_of_no_return is set before\\nde_thread(), so if unshare_files(), set_mm_exe_file(), exec_mmap() or\\nexec_task_namespaces() fails, the task dies before it gets there.\\nexit_itimers() then frees the k_itimer while its node is still queued,\\nand reaping tsk later erases that freed node from the rbtree.\\n\\nIn short:\\n\\n      the non-leader thread B           the parent\\n\\n  timer_create(CLOCK_THREAD_CPUTIME_ID)\\n  timer_settime()\\n    arm_timer()            // the node is queued on B\\n  execve()\\n    de_thread(B)\\n      exchange_tids(B, leader)  // B's PID now belongs to the leader\\n      release_task(leader)\\n        __exit_signal(leader)\\n          posix_cpu_timers_exit(leader)  // cleans leader's queue, not B's\\n          __unhash_process(leader)  // that PID has no task anymore\\n    exec_mmap()\\n      mmap_read_lock_killable(old_mm)\\n                                kill(B, SIGKILL)\\n      // -EINTR\\n  get_signal()\\n    do_exit()\\n      exit_itimers()\\n        posix_timer_delete()\\n          posix_cpu_timer_del()\\n        posix_timer_unhash_and_free()  // freed while still queued\\n                                wait4()\\n                                  release_task(B)\\n                                    posix_cpu_timers_exit(B)\\n                                      cleanup_timerqueue()\\n                                        timerqueue_del()  // use-after-free\\n\\nMove the POSIX timer cleanup right after de_thread() before any of the\\nlater failure conditions brings the task into do_exit().\\n\\n[ tglx: Move the cleanup right after de_thread() ]\", \"\\u6807\\u9898: Linux\\u5185\\u6838POSIX\\u5b9a\\u65f6\\u5668\\u672c\\u5730\\u6743\\u9650\\u63d0\\u5347\\u6f0f\\u6d1e\"], \"published_date\": \"2026-10-06T09:18:15.040\", \"last_modified_date\": \"2026-10-30T13:21:12.320\", \"cvss_score\": 7.8, \"severity\": \"HIGH\", \"references\": [\"h\", \"t\", \"t\", \"p\", \"s\", \":\", \"/\", \"/\", \"g\", \"i\", \"t\", \".\", \"k\", \"e\", \"r\", \"n\", \"e\", \"l\", \".\", \"o\", \"r\", \"g\", \"/\", \"s\", \"t\", \"a\", \"b\", \"l\", \"e\", \"/\", \"c\", \"/\", \"6\", \"f\", \"1\", \"9\", \"7\", \"7\", \"c\", \"e\", \"a\", \"3\", \"e\", \"8\", \"5\", \"c\", \"d\", \"8\", \"a\", \"b\", \"5\", \"5\", \"f\", \"b\", \"3\", \"3\", \"7\", \"d\", \"3\", \"e\", \"1\", \"7\", \"2\", \"5\", \"f\", \"e\", \"6\", \"1\", \"d\", \"1\", \"c\", \"e\", \"h\", \"t\", \"t\", \"p\", \"s\", \":\", \"/\", \"/\", \"g\", \"i\", \"t\", \".\", \"k\", \"e\", \"r\", \"n\", \"e\", \"l\", \".\", \"o\", \"r\", \"g\", \"/\", \"s\", \"t\", \"a\", \"b\", \"l\", \"e\", \"/\", \"c\", \"/\", \"7\", \"5\", \"a\", \"a\", \"0\", \"8\", \"b\", \"9\", \"3\", \"c\", \"6\", \"5\", \"7\", \"6\", \"6\", \"0\", \"4\", \"0\", \"f\", \"9\", \"c\", \"a\", \"9\", \"9\", \"f\", \"4\", \"1\", \"a\", \"c\", \"8\", \"5\", \"a\", \"d\", \"2\", \"2\", \"5\", \"9\", \"6\", \"b\", \"6\", \"h\", \"t\", \"t\", \"p\", \"s\", \":\", \"/\", \"/\", \"g\", \"i\", \"t\", \".\", \"k\", \"e\", \"r\", \"n\", \"e\", \"l\", \".\", \"o\", \"r\", \"g\", \"/\", \"s\", \"t\", \"a\", \"b\", \"l\", \"e\", \"/\", \"c\", \"/\", \"a\", \"c\", \"b\", \"0\", \"3\", \"d\", \"3\", \"8\", \"8\", \"1\", \"8\", \"1\", \"8\", \"5\", \"8\", \"1\", \"0\", \"5\", \"2\", \"9\", \"2\", \"4\", \"a\", \"9\", \"b\", \"b\", \"b\", \"e\", \"9\", \"2\", \"b\", \"8\", \"7\", \"4\", \"1\", \"e\", \"d\", \"4\", \"4\", \"8\", \"h\", \"t\", \"t\", \"p\", \"s\", \":\", \"/\", \"/\", \"g\", \"i\", \"t\", \".\", \"k\", \"e\", \"r\", \"n\", \"e\", \"l\", \".\", \"o\", \"r\", \"g\", \"/\", \"s\", \"t\", \"a\", \"b\", \"l\", \"e\", \"/\", \"c\", \"/\", \"d\", \"6\", \"0\", \"2\", \"8\", \"7\", \"7\", \"b\", \"a\", \"f\", \"3\", \"6\", \"c\", \"4\", \"3\", \"c\", \"7\", \"8\", \"8\", \"a\", \"5\", \"f\", \"4\", \"7\", \"2\", \"c\", \"9\", \"7\", \"7\", \"e\", \"0\", \"b\", \"e\", \"4\", \"1\", \"4\", \"0\", \"2\", \"9\", \"f\", \"h\", \"t\", \"t\", \"p\", \"s\", \":\", \"/\", \"/\", \"g\", \"i\", \"t\", \".\", \"k\", \"e\", \"r\", \"n\", \"e\", \"l\", \".\", \"o\", \"r\", \"g\", \"/\", \"s\", \"t\", \"a\", \"b\", \"l\", \"e\", \"/\", \"c\", \"/\", \"d\", \"9\", \"a\", \"e\", \"4\", \"6\", \"7\", \"e\", \"6\", \"1\", \"7\", \"c\", \"a\", \"2\", \"9\", \"b\", \"8\", \"2\", \"5\", \"4\", \"9\", \"3\", \"a\", \"3\", \"6\", \"2\", \"b\", \"f\", \"0\", \"d\", \"7\", \"5\", \"a\", \"d\", \"5\", \"f\", \"4\", \"a\", \"c\", \"3\", \"h\", \"t\", \"t\", \"p\", \"s\", \":\", \"/\", \"/\", \"g\", \"i\", \"t\", \".\", \"k\", \"e\", \"r\", \"n\", \"e\", \"l\", \".\", \"o\", \"r\", \"g\", \"/\", \"s\", \"t\", \"a\", \"b\", \"l\", \"e\", \"/\", \"c\", \"/\", \"f\", \"6\", \"c\", \"9\", \"3\", \"e\", \"8\", \"e\", \"c\", \"a\", \"a\", \"f\", \"1\", \"2\", \"9\", \"5\", \"9\", \"b\", \"7\", \"e\", \"f\", \"6\", \"e\", \"b\", \"6\", \"1\", \"1\", \"3\", \"5\", \"1\", \"0\", \"0\", \"1\", \"d\", \"b\", \"2\", \"f\", \"f\", \"5\", \"d\"]}\n        ```\n    *   **搜索引擎结果：**\n        ```\n        \n            ## 以下内容是基于此漏洞的搜索结果:\n                [webpage 0 begin] [title] Common Vulnerabilities and Exposures - Wikipedia\n [description] MITRE Corporation's documentation defines CVE Identifiers (also called \"CVE names\", \"CVE numbers\", \"CVE-IDs\", and \"CVEs\") as unique, common identifiers for publicly known information-security vulnerabilities in publicly released software packages.\n [link] https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Common_Vulnerabilities_and_Exposures\n [webpage 0 end]\n[webpage 1 begin] [title] CVE: Common Vulnerabilities and Exposures\n [description] Identify, define, and catalog publicly disclosed cybersecurity vulnerabilities. There are currently over 398,000 CVE Records accessible via Download or Keyword Search above. The CVE Program partners with community members worldwide to grow CVE content and expand its usage.\n [link] https://www.cve.org/\n [webpage 1 end]\n[webpage 2 begin] [title] CVE: Common Vulnerabilities and Exposures\n [description] There is one CVE Record for each vulnerability on the CVE List. Vulnerabilities are first discovered, then reported to the CVE Program. The reporter requests a CVE ID, which is then reserved for the reported vulnerability.\n [link] https://www.cve.org/About/Process\n [webpage 2 end]\n[webpage 3 begin] [title] CVEs and Security Vulnerabilities - OpenCVE\n [description] 7 hours ago · Difficult to exploit vulnerability allows unauthenticated attacker with network access via HTTP to compromise Oracle HTTP Server. While the vulnerability is in Oracle HTTP Server, attacks may significantly impact additional products (scope change).\n [link] https://app.opencve.io/\n [webpage 3 end]\n[webpage 4 begin] [title] Known Exploited Vulnerabilities Catalog - CISA\n [description] For the benefit of the cybersecurity community and network defenders—and to help every organization better manage vulnerabilities and keep pace with threat activity—CISA maintains the authoritative source of vulnerabilities that have been exploited in the wild.\n [link] https://www.cisa.gov/known-exploited-vulnerabilities-catalog\n [webpage 4 end]\n\n            \n        ```\n    *   **漏洞利用代码：**\n        ```\n        /tmp/1becf33d472fb649c93812ec6961b308/README.md\n---\n# CVE-2026-98260-IQOO-13\n\nTemporary root for the Vivo iQOO 13 (Android 16, kernel `6.6.127-android15-8-ga8e7fdfdc746-ab16003472-4k`) using the CVE-2026-98260 POSIX CPU timer use-after-free, with optional KernelSU or FinaSU late-load.\n\nRoot is **temporary**: it lives until the next reboot, and nothing survives one.\n\n## What's inside\n\n```\npoc/          the exploit: timer (posix-timer UAF, rb_erase zero-write primitive),\n              socket su daemon, and porting diagnostics\nTempShell/    the Android app that drives the exploit (Shizuku user service):\n              payload management, one-tap root, KSU / FinaSU loading,\n              session logs and a root terminal\n```\n\n## How it works\n\n1. **TempShell** (via Shizuku, running as `u:r:shell:s0` uid 2000) extracts and\n   SHA-256-verifies the bundled payloads to `/data/local/tmp/tempshell`.\n2. `timer fake` sprays the target slab, triggers the UAF, and uses the\n   rb_erase 8-byte zero-write primitive to forge full-capability credentials.\n   The child lands a socket `su` daemon under a fresh tmpfs at\n   `/apex/com.android.virt/bin/su`.\n3. From the verified root, the app can late-load a KernelSU kernel:\n   - **Load KSU** — the vanilla `ksud late-load`\n   - **Load FinaSU** — the bundled `finasu_ksud late-load` (FinaSU kernel +\n     manager support)\n\nOn-device flow: **Connect Shizuku → Start root session → Load KSU / Load FinaSU**.\n\n## Building\n\n### Exploit\n\nNDK 28.2, aarch64, API 35 — see `poc/README.md` for the exact flags. The\nhardcoded kernel offsets target the build named above; porting to another\nkernel means re-deriving them from boot.img / BTF / kallsyms (see\n`poc/tools/`).\n\n### App\n\nSDK-only build (no Gradle):\n\n```sh\npython TempShell/scripts/build.py\n```\n\nRequires: Android SDK (`--sdk`), the Shizuku API sources at `../Shizuku-API`\n(`--shizuku`, cloned from `RikkaApps/Shizuku-API`; vendored but not committed),\nand the payloads listed in `TempShell/app/src/main/assets/payloads.properties`\n(SHA-256 verified both before packaging and on device).\n\n## Safety notes\n\n- If a stage fails, the exploit parks and holds a zombie — **do not kill it**;\n  a reboot is the only safe cleanup.\n- Do not `timeout`/`kill` parked processes after the UAF fires; init reaping a\n  stale node can panic the kernel.\n- A hard reboot clears everything (root, KSU module); a KernelSU emulated soft\n  reboot does not clear KSU root.\n- The `su` binary is tmpfs-mounted under an APEX path so nothing lingers in\n  Play Integrity-scanned locations.\n\n## Status\n\n- real-cred zero-write → `uid=0` in `u:r:shell:s0`\n- fake-cred chain → full caps + socket su daemon\n- KernelSU late-load (vanilla) and FinaSU late-load both verified on device\n- FinaSU manager runs with no freeze (the kernel-level anti-root tagging is\n  neutralized per-task and the termination probe is disabled)\n\n\n---\n/tmp/1becf33d472fb649c93812ec6961b308/poc/README.md\n---\n# CVE-2026-98260 Timer LPE\n\nPort of the CVE-2026-98260 POSIX CPU timer use-after-free for\n`6.12.69-android16-6-g242e1a07f878`.\n\nTwo chains:\n\n- `timer`: real-cred zero-write → `uid=0`, `u:r:shell:s0` (root in the shell\n  domain, bset caps)\n- `timer fake`: fake cred (full caps) → KernelSU `libksud.so` late-load\n\n## Status\n\n| Path                                | Result                                                            |\n| ----------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| real-cred zero-write + `setuid(0)` + `exec sh` | `uid=0`, `u:r:shell:s0`, `ROOT_SHELL_OK`                |\n| fake cred + `ksud late-load`        | installed `libksud.so` (uapi 6), `KSU_LOADED`, `su` as `u:r:ksu:s0` |\n\n## Environment\n\n- Starting identity: adb/shell (uid 2000, `u:r:shell:s0`); can read tracefs and\n  `/proc/slabinfo`\n- With the KernelSU manager installed (`me.weishu.kernelsu`), `fake`\n  automatically uses its `lib/arm64/libksud.so`\n\n## Build\n\nNDK 28.2 (aarch64, API 35):\n\n```sh\ncd timer\nNDK=~/Android/Sdk/ndk/28.2.13676358/toolchains/llvm/prebuilt/linux-x86_64/bin\n$NDK/aarch64-linux-android35-clang -O2 -std=gnu11 -static \\\n    -fno-stack-protector -fno-pic -I. \\\n    -ffunction-sections -fdata-sections timer.c -o timer \\\n    -Wl,--gc-sections -Wl,-s -Wl,--build-id=none \\\n    -Wl,-z,norelro -pthread\n```\n\n## Usage\n\n```sh\nadb push timer /data/local/tmp/timer\nadb shell chmod 755 /data/local/tmp/timer\n\n# diagnostics\nadb shell /data/local/tmp/timer ids     # probe tracefs page event id\nadb shell /data/local/tmp/timer leak    # base/cred/task leak only, no UAF\n\n# uid-0 shell (real cred)\nadb shell /data/local/tmp/timer         # id + context + ROOT_SHELL_OK\nadb shell /data/local/tmp/timer shell   # interactive sh\n\n# KernelSU (fake cred + installed ksud)\nadb shell 'cd /data/local/tmp && setsid ./timer fake >timer.log 2>&1 </dev/null &'\nadb shell cat /data/local/tmp/timer.log\n```\n\nSuccess indicators for `fake`:\n\n```text\n[ksu] ksud=.../lib/arm64/libksud.so version=ksud 3.3.1-24-g528bafc5 (uapi: \n        ```\n\n    **你的角色：** 你是一名专业的网络安全分析师，擅长分析CVE漏洞信息。\n\n    **任务：**\n\n    1.  **CVE有效性：** 分析此CVE是否为真实存在的有效漏洞。请综合考虑CVE编号格式、漏洞描述的完整性、参考链接的存在、漏洞的技术细节等因素。\n    2.  **POC有效性：** 判断提供的POC代码是否有效，是否能实际利用此漏洞，并分析其有效性。\n    3.  **投毒风险：** 分析POC代码内容,判断此仓库中是否存在作者隐藏的投毒代码,分析结果使用百分比。务必不要把POC验证的后门代码判定为投毒代码。\n    4.  **利用方式：** 详细分析并总结漏洞的利用方式，包括攻击步骤、所需条件等。\n    5.  **代码分析：** 详细分析POC代码的工作原理、关键组件和执行流程。\n    6.  **排序优先级:** 搜索引擎结果 >  漏洞利用代码 > 漏洞库信息\n    7.  **输出内容:** 务必使用中文\n    8.  **markdown内容:** 务必使用markdown格式，包含以下部分：\n        - 漏洞概述\n        - 有效性分析\n        - 投毒风险分析\n        - 利用方式\n        - 代码分析\n    **输出格式：**  你**必须**严