cluded as a convenience;\n   ONLY the wheels-based path was exercised end-to-end by the delivery\n   and the same-version installed twins were verified equivalent by hash,\n   the online path is supplied for reachability, NOT as a re-verified claim.\n   An evaluator who needs a re-verified build should use the same\n   instructions as `lab-recipe.md` for the pinned build.\n3. **Manifest exclusion surfaces.** `BUNDLE.sha256` lists project-root and\n   lab paths unhashed per name: `01_research/src` (pinned clones),\n   `lab/wheels/` (3.2 GB wheels), `lab/venv` (host venv), and the\n   self-referencing audit row. The published copy is a redacted subset;\n   the full internal record stays under private validation-hold.\n4. **Exit-code contract note.** Row \"1 = sent, target unresponsive\" is\n   documented but not reachable in current probe paths — the drivers\n   return 0/3 (probe) or 0/2/3 (-c mode). The table carries an explicit\n   `[contract not reachable in current paths]` annotation.\n5. **A capture-harness repair is part of this release.** The matrix leg 2\n   verdict is now rc-gated (PASS requires a controlled refusal + marker\n   absent + `msgspec.ValidationError` receipt): the pre-fix harness could\n   let a half-up lab \"pass\" the patched leg; contrapositive repro is in\n   the internal fixlog. The new `16-15-matrix-v4.txt` row is the\n   corrected capture; `12-11` is marked SUPERSEDED in `evidence/INDEX.txt`.\n\n\n---\n/tmp/35ce3cc9b72e8baddce2450323930620/MANIFEST.txt\n---\n40ea881c5a7ed996a9c863763272e4b39593f4c009f4c820497116109a2d9e9b  KNOWN-GAPS.md\nfe72921e70dcfb9ca0c2bc333eb72eb26cd5f407af2bc044a216fd673be082c0  README.md\n369596bf55c6f080a4aedacb60590f167b156a3ffb63812ed0df9b36b46f7354  STATE.md\n8821bf7b4f4fc13faff83fbd48a496bce0b7c2833ed25fc5828affd3b7dff019  evidence/01-01-environment.txt\n24c9085f7a7886803c2c250d43ea8ce418fe2b6e3607ba06b9f5a5918b9d8c46  evidence/02-02-trigger.txt\n4aba10449236f7957dc8dbf11c954846273fdc23e84820a6d18863cdcd88546c