  ```\n        /tmp/6e54b570325fbf61f8cebf50f5722bdb/LICENSE\n---\nMIT License\n\nCopyright (c) 2026 Fromagegate Research & Defense Collective\n\nPermission is hereby granted, free of charge, to any person obtaining a copy\nof this software and associated documentation files (the \"Software\"), to deal\nin the Software without restriction, including without limitation the rights\nto use, copy, modify, merge, publish, distribute, sublicense, and/or sell\ncopies of the Software, and to permit persons to whom the Software is\nfurnished to do so, subject to the following conditions:\n\nThe above copyright notice and this permission notice shall be included in all\ncopies or substantial portions of the Software.\n\nTHE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED \"AS IS\", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR\nIMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY,\nFITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE AND NONINFRINGEMENT. IN NO EVENT SHALL THE\nAUTHORS OR COPYRIGHT HOLDERS BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES OR OTHER\nLIABILITY, WHETHER IN AN ACTION OF CONTRACT, TORT OR OTHERWISE, ARISING FROM,\nOUT OF OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE SOFTWARE OR THE USE OR OTHER DEALINGS IN THE\nSOFTWARE.\n\n\n---\n/tmp/6e54b570325fbf61f8cebf50f5722bdb/README.md\n---\n# CVE-2025-41450 & The \"Fromagegate\" Incident\n### Technical Post-Mortem, Vulnerability Analysis, and OT Cyber-Physical Defense Blueprint\n\n[![License: MIT](https://img.shields.io/badge/License-MIT-yellow.svg)](https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT)\n[![Vulnerability: CVE-2025-41450](https://img.shields.io/badge/CVE-2025--41450-critical.svg)](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2025-41450)\n[![Target: Danfoss AK-SM 8xxA](https://img.shields.io/badge/OT%20Target-Danfoss%20AK--SM%208xxA-blue.svg)](https://www.danfoss.com)\n[![Incident: French Supermarket Sabotage](https://img.shields.io/badge/Incident-October%202026%20Fromagegate-red.svg)](docs/incident-report-october-2026.md)\n[![Advisory: CERTFR-2026-ALE-012](https://img.shields.io/badge/CERT--FR-CERTFR--2026--ALE--012-orange.svg)](docs/remediation-and-hardening.md)\n\n---\n\n## 📌 Executive Summary\n\nIn October 2026, an unprecedented cyber-physical sabotage campaign—dubbed **\"Fromagegate\"** by the cybersecurity community—struck more than **700 commercial supermarkets** across France and parts of Western Europe (affecting major retail chains including Intermarché, Carrefour, Coopérative U, Monoprix, and E.Leclerc). \n\nRather than deploying ransomware for financial extortion or exfiltrating customer records, malicious threat actors directly hijacked internet-exposed **Operational Technology (OT)** refrigeration controllers—predominantly the **Danfoss AK-SM 8xxA Series System Managers** running the *StoreView* web interface.\n\nBy abusing **CVE-2025-41450** (an improper authentication bypass flaw rooted in a predictable \"Code-of-the-Day\" derivation algorithm), attackers gained administrative control without credentials and remotely forced industrial cooling units into continuous **defrost cycles**. Temperatures inside refrigerated displays and cold-storage rooms surged from normal temperatures (-18°C to +4°C) to as high as **+50°C (122°F)**. \n\nThe physical consequences were catastrophic:\n* **Tens of millions of euros** in spoiled meat, dairy, produce, and frozen food inventory.\n* Localized equipment overheating, electrical smoke, and minor fire alarms in multiple facilities.\n* Severe supply-chain disruption and emergency operational alerts issued by national cyber agencies (**CERT-FR alert CERTFR-2026-ALE-012**).\n\nThis repository provides a comprehensive technical retrospective, architecture diagrams, vulnerability mechanics, safe local educational simulation, detection telemetry (Suricata/Sigma), and hardening blueprints.\n\n---\n\n## 📂 Repository Structure\n\n```tree\ncve-2025-41450-fromagegate/\n├── README.md                              <- Main project overview and technical summary\n├── docs/\n│   ├── vulnerability-analysis.md          <- Detailed algorithmic & protocol flaw analysis\n│   ├── incident-report-october-2026.md    <- Timeline, physical impact, and retail case study\n│   └── remediation-and-hardening.md       <- Network isolation & Purdue model blueprint\n├── simulator/\n│   ├── controller_simulator.py            <- Safe, local educational Python mock (port 8080)\n│   └── audit_check.py                     <- Non-destructive defensive compliance scanner\n└── detections/\n    ├── suricata.rules                     <- Network IDS/IPS detection signatures\n    ├── sigma_rules.yml                    <- SIEM/Sigma rules for StoreView tampering\n    └── shodan_censys_queries.md           <- Defensive exposure hunting queries\n```\n\n---\n\n## 🔍 The Vulnerability Chain at a Glance\n\nThe Danfoss AK-SM 800A controller series (extensively researched by **Claroty Team82** in their research paper *\"Freeze the Controller, Defrost the Food\"*) was subject to a three-stage vulnerability chain:\n\n| CVE ID | Type | CVSS v3.1 | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **CVE-2025-41450** | **Authentication Bypass** \n        ```\n\n    **你的角色：** 你是一名专业的网络安全分析师，擅长分析CVE漏洞信息。\n\n    **任务：**\n\n    1.  **CVE有效性：** 分析此CVE是否为真实存在的有效漏洞。请综合考虑CVE编号格式、漏洞描述的完整性、参考链接的存在、漏洞的技术细节等因素。\n    2.  **POC有效性：** 判断提供的POC代码是否有效，是否能实际利用此漏洞，并分析其有效性。\n    3.  **投毒风险：** 分析POC代码内容,判断此仓库中是否存在作者隐藏的投毒代码,分析结果使用百分比。务必不要把POC验证的后门代码判定为投毒代码。\n    4.  **利用方式：** 详细分析并总结漏洞的利用方式，包括攻击步骤、所需条件等。\n    5.  **代码分析：** 详细分析POC代码的工作原理、关键组件和执行流程。\n    6.  **排序优先级:** 搜索引擎结果 >  漏洞利用代码 > 漏洞库信息\n    7.  **输出内容:** 务必使用中文\n    8.  **markdown内容:** 务必使用markdown格式，包含以下部分：\n        - 漏洞概述\n        - 有效性分析\n        - 投毒风险分析\n        - 利用方式\n        - 代码分析\n    **输出格式：**  你**必须**严格按照以下 **JSON** 格式输出，**不要包含任何额外的文字、说明或前缀/后缀**。JSON中的**所有键和字符串类型的值必须使用双引号**。请务必对特殊字符进行转义。\n\n    **示例JSON:**```json\n    {\n        \"name\": \"CVE-2023-12345-ExampleApp-SQL注入\",\n        \"type\": \"SQL注入\",\n        \"app\": \"ExampleApp\", \n        \"risk\": \"高危，可能导致数据泄露和远程代码执行\",\n        \"version\": \"<= 1.0\",\n        \"condition\": \"需要网络访问和数据库端口开放\",\n        \"poc_available\": \"是\",\n        \"poison\": \"90%\",\n        \"cve_valid\": \"是\",\n        \"markdown\": \"# 漏洞概述\n\n该漏洞存在于ExampleApp的登录模块,攻击者可以通过构造恶意的SQL语句绕过身份验证...\n\n## 有效性分析\n\n根据CVE编号格式、漏洞描述的完整性、参考链接的存在等因素，该CVE是真实有效的...\n\n## 投毒风险分析\n\n该仓库存在较高的投毒风险，主要原因是...\n\n## 利用方式\n\n1.  攻击者需要网络访问权限\n2.  构造恶意的SQL语句\n3.  发送到目标系统\n4.  绕过身份验证，获取系统访问权限\n\n## 代码分析\n\n主要代码组件包括：\n- `exploit.py`: 主漏洞利用脚本\n- `payloads.py`: 包含各种SQL注入payload\n- `utils.py`: 辅助工具函数\n\n代码执行流程：\n1.  连接到目标数据库\n2.  构造恶意SQL语句\n3.  发送到目标系统\n4.  解析响应，获取敏感信息\n\",\n        \"repo_name\": \"example/repo\",\n        \"repo_url\": \"https://github.com/example/repo\",\n        \"cve_url\": \"https://cve.mitre.org/cgi-bin/cvename.cgi?name=CVE-2023-12345\"\n    }\n        ",
